    92	so `Q=eta^{-m}(1+U)` and `etat=eta(1+U)^{-1/m}`, hence
    93	
    94	```text
    95	P*etat^{n} = (1+U)^{-n/m}.
    96	```
    97	
    98	Suppose `U = U_4 + U_bad` with `U_4` supported on `4Z` and `ord_eta U_bad = M_2+m`.
    99	Then `(1+U)^{-n/m} = (1+U_4)^{-n/m} * (1 + U_bad/(1+U_4))^{-n/m}`, whose first
   100	non-`4Z` exponent is `M_2+m` with coefficient `-(n/m) q_{M_2} != 0`
   101	(the `U_bad^2` correction has order `2(M_2+m)`). The substitution
   102	`eta -> etat = eta*(4Z-supported)*(1+O(eta^{M_2+m}))` preserves `4Z`-support and
   103	scales that coefficient by a unit. Since `4 | n`, the `etat`-exponent
   104	`M_2+m` corresponds to `p_j` with `j+n=M_2+m`, i.e.
   105	
   106	```text
   107	N = M_2-(n-m) = m-3 = 8t+1,        M_2+m = 20t+5 = 5(4t+1).
   108	```
